(a) the number and percentage of undertrial prisoners in the country during the last three years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the number and percentage of undertrial prisoners who have availed free legal aid during the same period, State-wise;
(c) whether Government maintains data on undertrial prisoners disaggregated by SC, ST, OBC and minority categories and if so, the details thereof;
(d) if not, whether Government proposes to collect and publish it to assess disparities in access to justice; and
(e) the specific measures taken to ensure timely legal representation and prevent prolonged detention of undertrial prisoners?

(a) the number of Indian fishermen detained, injured and killed by the authorities/individuals of neighbouring countries during the last three years, year-wise and country-wise;
(b) whether the Ministry has data on the number of such fishermen who have been repatriated, those still under detention and the compensation or assistance extended to the affected families;
(c) whether Government has taken up the issue with the neighbouring countries to prevent recurrence of such incidents and to secure the early release of detained fishermen; and
(d) the measures taken by Government to ensure the safety and legal protection  of Indian fishermen operating in border maritime areas?

SR

(a) the sanctioned strength and the number of persons in position in the Ministry and its CPSEs, organisation-wise, as on date;
(b) the number of appointments made against sanctioned posts during the last four years, year-wise and organisation-wise;
(c) whether Government has conducted any manpower assessment to determine the adequacy of staffing for operation and maintenance of power infrastructure, and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken to address manpower shortages in the Ministry and its CPSEs?

(a) the sanctioned strength and working strength in the Petroleum and Explosives Safety Organisation (PESO); 
(b) whether Government has assessed the impact of manpower shortages in PESO on inspection, safety audits and enforcement activities, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the number of inspections of petroleum, explosives and compressed gas installations carried out by PESO during the last five years, year-wise; and 
(d) whether Government proposes to undertake a comprehensive review of the manpower requirements of PESO in view of the increasing number of establishments under its regulatory jurisdiction, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the area of forest land diverted for non-forest purposes and the number of trees approved for felling during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the sector-wise details of such approvals, including mining, infrastructure, industries and other development projects;
(c) whether Government has conducted any assessment of the ecological impact of such  diversion of forest land and tree felling and if so, the details thereof;
(d) the details of compensatory afforestation undertaken against such approvals during the same period, including the area afforested and survival rate of plantations, State-wise; and
(e) the measures taken by Government to minimise diversion of forest land?

(a) the number of cases initiated and the amount recovered under the Securitisation and Reconstruction of Financial Assets and Enforcement of Security Interest Act, 2002 (SARFAESI)  during the last three years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) number of borrowers against whom proceedings were initiated under the Act during the said period, indicating the number belonging to Below Poverty Line, Scheduled Castes, Scheduled Tribes and Other Backward Classes, State-wise;
(c) whether Government has conducted any assessment of the socio-economic impact of SARFAESI proceedings on low-income borrowers, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) safeguards and relief measures to protect economically weaker borrowers from undue hardship during proceedings under the SARFAESI Act?

(a) the number of inspections conducted and notices issued by the FSSAI to quick-commerce platforms and their dark stores during the last four years, year-wise and company-wise;
(b) the number of cases involving storage or sale of expired, spoiled, mislabelled or otherwise unsafe food products detected during the said period, along with the action taken thereon;
(c) whether Government has conducted any assessment of food safety compliance in the quick-commerce sector and if so, the details and key findings thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to strengthen monitoring and ensure compliance with food safety standards by quick-commerce platforms and their associated warehouses?

(a) the quantity of ethanol produced in the country during the last five years, company-wise and year-wise, indicating Public Sector and Private Sector companies separately;
(b) the details of profit earned by each ethanol-producing Public Sector and Private Sector company during the last five years, year-wise;
(c) whether Government has assessed the reasons for the comparatively lower production and capacity utilisation, if any, in Public Sector companies engaged in ethanol production and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken by Government to enhance ethanol production and operational efficiency in Public Sector companies?

(a) whether Government has assessed the impact of  mandatory use of digital applications on the implementation of Viksit Bharat—Guarantee for Rozgar and Ajeevika Mission (Gramin) (VB—G RAM G); 
(b) the number of instances reported during the last three years where technical or application-related issues affected attendance recording, wage payments or work allocation, State-wise;
(c) whether Government has conducted any assessment of the number of workers who were unable to avail employment or experienced delays in wage payments due to such digital issues; and
(d) the corrective measures taken to ensure that technical failures or digital authentication issues do not deprive eligible workers of employment or timely payment of wages?

(a) whether Government has assessed the impact of Labour Codes on employment security, contractual employment, retrenchment and layoffs since their implementation and if so, the findings thereof;
(b) the number of establishments that retrenched workers, laid off employees or closed operations under the Labour Codes, State-wise and sector-wise;
(c) whether any comparative study has been undertaken on retrenchments, layoffs, industrial disputes and formal employment before and after the implementation of Labour Codes; and
(d) whether Government proposes an independent review of implementation of Labour Codes and its impact on workers' rights and employment security?

(a) the number of vacancies requisitioned by various Ministries/Departments to the Staff Selection Commission (SSC) and the number of candidates recommended by it during the last four years, year-wise and Ministry/Department-wise;
(b) the sanctioned strength and the number of persons in position in the posts filled through SSC, Ministry/Department-wise, as on 1st July, 2026;
(c) whether any Ministries/Departments have reported delays in filling requisitioned posts through SSC during the last four years and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken by Government to reduce the gap between sanctioned strength and persons in position in posts filled through SSC?

(a) the details of funds allocated, released and utilised by the Central Government for mitigation of human–wildlife conflict during the last four years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the details of project proposals received from Government of Kerala during those years for mitigation of human–wildlife conflict, along with their present status;
(c) whether any such proposals are pending with the Central Government and if so, the reasons for the delay in their approval; and 
(d) the steps taken by Government to expedite approval of pending proposals and strengthen measures for mitigation of human–wildlife conflict in vulnerable regions?

J

(a) whether the Ministry has conducted any assessment of the impact of 20 percent ethanol-blended petrol (E20) on vehicle performance, fuel efficiency, engine durability and maintenance costs and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether the Ministry has received complaints regarding the same and if so, the action taken thereon;
(c) whether the Ministry consulted automobile manufacturers, component manufacturers, transport operators, consumer organisations and other stakeholders before the nationwide rollout of E20 fuel and if so, the details and recommendations thereof; and
(d) the steps taken to address the concerns of vehicle owners to ensure better vehicle performance, safety and fuel efficiency?

(a) whether the Union Government has taken follow-up action for the establishment of an All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) in Kerala after the State Government identified and allotted land for the project in Kozhikode district, and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the present status of the proposal, including the preliminary works completed by the Union Government;
(c) the reasons for the delay in obtaining the necessary approvals and commencing construction of AIIMS in Kerala; and
(d) the timeline fixed by Government for completion of the preliminary formalities and commencement of construction of AIIMS in Kerala?

(a) the details of agencies, other than the CISF, engaged for airport security, passenger facilitation and queue management at airports in the country, airport-wise;
(b) nature of duties assigned to each such agency and the authority under which they have been engaged;
(c) whether any instances of mismanagement, negligence or violation of prescribed procedures by such agencies have come to the notice of Government during the last five years, airport-wise and the action taken thereon; and
(d) the mechanism in place to monitor performance, accountability and training of such agencies to ensure passenger safety and efficient airport operations?

(a) the Vande Bharat trains which maintained high occupancy during the last year, train-wise;
(b) whether Government has assessed the requirement for additional Vande Bharat and other high-speed train services in Kerala based on the occupancy of the existing services;
(c) whether the Ministry has prescribed any occupancy benchmark or demand criteria for introducing additional Vande Bharat services and whether the existing Vande Bharat services in Kerala satisfy such criteria; and
(d) whether Government proposes to introduce additional train services in Kerala in view of the consistently high occupancy of the existing services, if so, the details and timeline thereof?

(a) the number of cases of mass layoffs, retrenchments and closures reported in private sector establishments during the last five years, year-wise, State-wise and sector-wise;
(b) whether Government has conducted any assessment of the reasons behind increasing instances of mass layoffs in private sector and if so, the details and findings thereof;
(c) the number of workers affected by such layoffs and the measures taken by Government to facilitate their re-employment and social security; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to regulate mass layoffs, strengthen employment security and ensure compliance with labour laws by private sector establishments?

(a) whether Government has assessed the impact of inadequate internet connectivity and digital infrastructure on the implementation of Anganwadi services, particularly in rural and tribal areas;
(b) the number of Anganwadi centres lacking adequate internet connectivity and digital devices required for implementation of digital applications, State-wise;
(c) whether Government has received representations regarding difficulties faced by Anganwadi workers due to mandatory use of digital applications and the action taken thereon; and
(d) the steps taken to bridge the digital divide and ensure uninterrupted delivery of Anganwadi services?

(a) the details of funds allocated, released and utilised for the development of National Waterways during the last three years, Waterway-wise and State-wise;
(b) the present status of all National Waterway projects in Kerala;
(c) whether Government has identified delays in the implementation of National Waterway projects in Kerala and if so, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the timeline fixed for completion of the pending National Waterway projects in Kerala and the steps taken to expedite their completion?

(a) the number of deaths attributable to medical errors reported in the country during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the number of serious physical disabilities or injuries caused by medical errors during the same period, year-wise and State-wise;
(c) whether a centralised database exists for reporting, investigation and classification of such cases, with details;
(d) the financial assistance, compensation, ex gratia or legal support provided by the Union Government, including amounts disbursed; and
(e) the specific measures taken to strengthen patient safety protocols, clinical audits and error-prevention systems in public and private healthcare institutions?

(a) the number of enterprises registered on the Udyam Portal during the last three years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the number of MSMEs that ceased operations during the last three years, year-wise and State-wise;
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of the recent shortage in LPG on MSME closures and resulting job loss and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, whether Government is ready to conduct a study on the impact of LPG shortage on MSMEs, including business closures and job losses?

(a) the total domestic production of Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) and the quantity of LPG imported during each of the last five years, year-wise;
(b) whether Government has detected cases of black marketing or diversion of domestic LPG during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise, and the action taken thereon;
(c) the steps taken to prevent the black marketing of the LPG; and
(d) the measures taken to strengthen domestic LPG availability and prevent future supply disruptions?

(a) details of surcharge and additional fare levied  over and above the base airfare;
(b) whether Government has examined that the surcharge and additional charges levied by airlines are commensurate with the prevailing prices of ATF and other operating costs, and if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government has noticed that reductions in crude oil or ATF prices were not correspondingly reflected in the  additional charges collected by airlines, and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government proposes to issue any guidelines or establish a mechanism to ensure that reductions in ATF prices are reflected in airfares and additional charges levied?

(a) the number of cases registered during the last five years wherein industries were found to have disposed of waste into river bodies or public spaces, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the types of pollutants and scale of pollution identified;
(c) the actions taken against defaulting industries during the said period;
(d) the preventive and compliance measures taken to curb industrial discharge into water bodies and public spaces, including monitoring systems and guidance issued to industries; and
(e) whether any assessment has been conducted on persistent non-compliance and repeated violations, and if so, the findings thereof?

(a) the number of Gram Panchayats in the country that currently have permanent internet connectivity, State-wise;
(b) whether the Union Government has implemented any scheme or programme to provide internet connectivity to Panchayats and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the funds allocated and released for this purpose during the last five years, State-wise and year-wise; and
(d) if no such scheme exists or where gaps remain, whether Government proposes to introduce new schemes or initiatives to ensure reliable internet connectivity in all Panchayats?

(a) whether the Ministry has conducted any assessment of price volatility and income distress faced by farmers cultivating plantation and spice crops such as pepper, rubber and cardamom during the last five years;
(b) the details of the average farm-gate prices of these crops vis-à-vis the cost of cultivation during the same period;
(c) whether any proposals or representations have been received from State Governments or farmers’ organisations seeking inclusion of these crops under MSP or assured procurement mechanism; and
(d) whether Government proposes to examine the feasibility of extending MSP or any alternative price-stabilisation mechanism for pepper, rubber and cardamom?

(a) the details of funds allocated and released for providing TA and DA to Anganwadi workers and helpers for attending monthly review meetings during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) whether the provision for payment of TA and DA to Anganwadi workers and helpers has been discontinued by Government and, if so, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government has received any representations from States, Anganwadi workers or their organisations regarding the discontinuation of TA and DA; and
(d) whether Government is ready to review the decision and restore the provision of TA and DA for Anganwadi workers and helpers?

(a) the details of the gross household financial savings in the country and its share in GDP during each of the last five financial years, year-wise;
(b) the details of household financial liabilities, including borrowings from banks, Non-Banking Financial Companies, both in absolute terms and as a percentage of GDP year-wise;
(c) whether any study has been conducted on the reasons behind the increase in household liabilities and the decline in savings, if so, the details and findings thereof;
(d) if not, whether Government proposes to undertake such a study; and
(e) the steps taken to address declining household savings and rising liabilities?

(a) the total funds allocated and released by the Ministry for Ayurvedic research centres and institutions during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the criteria adopted for allocation of financial assistance to Ayurvedic research institutions across States;
(c) whether the Ministry is reviewing the proposals submitted by Government of Kerala seeking financial assistance for strengthening Ayurvedic research infrastructure in the State;
(d) if so, the present status of such proposals, including the stage of examination and expected timeline for decision; and
(e) whether there has been any delay in sanctioning assistance, if so, the reasons therefor and the steps taken to expedite the process?

SR

(a) the details of availability of electricity and the extent of load shedding reported in urban and rural areas during the last three years, State-wise and year-wise ;
(b) whether there are significant disparities in the availability and reliability of electricity supply between urban and rural areas and, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the reasons for load shedding reported in various States during the said period, including shortages in generation, transmission constraints and distribution-related issues; and
(d) the steps taken and assistance given by Government to ensure an uninterrupted and reliable electricity supply in both urban and rural areas across the country?

(a) the total revenue earned by the Indian Railways from deductions on automatically cancelled tickets during the last five financial years, year-wise;
(b) the number of tickets that were automatically cancelled in each of these years;
(c) the average percentage or amount retained by the Railways on automatic cancellations as per current reservation rules and notification;
(d) whether the Ministry has assessed the cumulative financial burden imposed on ordinary passengers due to such charges and deduction practices, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) whether Government proposes to revise the current fare-deduction and refund framework to ensure equitable treatment of passengers?

SR

(a) the number of pending cases in the Supreme Court and each High Court as on date, during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the number of civil and criminal cases pending separately in each of these courts;
(c) whether the Ministry has identified specific reasons for the rise in judicial pendency, including vacancies of judges; and
(d) the measures being taken to reduce pendency and ensure timely disposal of cases in the higher judiciary?

(a) the number of cases of physical attack  against women and children during each of the last three years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the number of cyber crime incidents recorded against women and children during the same period, year-wise and State-wise;
(c) the number of such cases that resulted in arrests, prosecutions and convictions, with outcomes and pendency figures, year-wise;
(d) whether the Ministry has conducted any analysis to identify trends, common platforms or modalities in cyber offences targeting women and children; and
(e) the specific policy measures, interventions, capacity-building efforts and coordination mechanisms put in place by Government?

(a) the total number of students selected for the  National Fellowship for Other Backward Classes (NFOBC) scholarship in each of the last three academic years, year-wise;
(b) the total amount allocated and released for disbursement under the NFOBC scheme during the same period and the amount pending for release, year-wise;
(c) the number of students who have reported delays in receiving fellowship stipends or tuition support with an estimate of average delay duration; and
(d) whether the Ministry has conducted a review of procedural bottlenecks or administrative gaps responsible for these delays and the steps proposed to ensure the timely release of funds to OBC PhD scholars?

(a) the quantity of Rice allocated under the Annapoorna Scheme during each of the last four years, year-wise and State-wise;
(b) the number of beneficiaries covered under the Annapoorna Scheme during the same period, State-wise and year-wise;
(c) whether Government has examined the eligibility criteria for the scheme, particularly the provision that persons receiving old age pension are excluded from coverage, if so, the findings of such examination; and
(d) whether Government is ready to modify the eligibility criteria to remove conditions that exclude elderly persons receiving old age pensions?

(a) total number of proposals received from State Governments under the PMJVK during the last five years, State-wise and year-wise, and the number of proposals currently pending for approval;
(b) the State-wise details of funds received by the respective State Governments under PMJVK against their demands;
(c) the number of proposals submitted by Government of Kerala that are pending approval, along with the total financial outlay involved;
(d) the reasons for the delay in approving the proposals submitted by Government of Kerala; and
(e) whether Government proposes to approve the pending proposals by Government of Kerala?

(a) whether the Ministry has reviewed the safety standards of mobile phones and related communications devices sold and used in India, including any tests conducted for radiation, battery safety, network compatibility and consumer harm;
(b) the number of device models tested, the criteria used and the results classified by manufacturer and year for the last three years;
(c) whether any hazards, non-compliance or safety risks have been identified, if so, the action taken against manufacturers or importers in such cases; and
(d) the steps being taken to strengthen regulatory oversight and consumer grievance redressal mechanisms?

